                                        "entry_id": "4058566c-a726-35a9-b385-e76f1ff190b4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of many aquatic photosynthetic organisms, including the seaweeds, whose size ranges from a single cell to giant kelps and whose biochemistry and forms are very diverse, some being eukaryotic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53b785b1-8346-4bbb-8198-fffa619da431",
                                                "sense_id": "7787c982-d739-3062-b3f1-7eb6188bd2b6",
                                                "text": "For example, the antitumour depsipeptide kahalalide F was isolated from the opisthobranch mollusc Elysia rufescens, and is used by both the mollusc and its dietary alga Bryopsis spp."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
